 34SI c  2002Mi44, 2002Mi48: a 55-MeV/nucleon {+34}Si secondary beam was        
 34SI2c  produced via fragmentation of a {+36}S primary beam at GANIL. The beam 
 34SI3c  was transported to the SPEG reaction chamber and was stopped in a      
 34SI4c  telescope of |DE and E silicon detectors. Isomeric internal conversion 
 34SI5c  electrons were detected by a 3500-|mm Si(Li) detector followed the Si  
 34SI6c  telescope. |g rays were detected with a 4|p array consisting of 72     
 34SI7c  BaF{-2} detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, (particle)-|g-coin, and          
 34SI8c  population cross sections.                                             
 34SI c  No evidence for a low-lying shape isomeric 0+ state was found in 34Si, 
 34SI2c  and an upper limit for the population cross-section could be           
 34SI3c  established                                                            
